    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0817" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/8–1444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-08-14">August 14, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Shang Chen, head of the Chinese Military Mission, Dr. H. H. Kung, and the
                    Chinese Ambassador called at their request. <pb facs="0818" n="804"
                        xml:id="pg804"/> They were somewhat put out at the report that Russia was
                    opposed to having concurrent security conversations by the two groups of three
                    nations each that are to discuss informally the security problems and proposals.
                    I again reviewed just what I had done in an effort to be of help to China and
                    concluded by saying that the Russians on their own initiative expressed their
                    opposition to having concurrent meetings. I said that this made clear the need
                    for better relations between the two countries of Russia and China and I favored
                    this, as I had been saying since I was at Moscow, without reference to the
                    question of whose fault the present situation was.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
